[{:db/id 17592186115355 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7a104075-f533-58ab-b79b-2a5e66b667e2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115356 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b8302ddf-29cf-570b-b7dd-dab545b3b824"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b8302ddf-29cf-570b-b7dd-dab545b3b824" :question/id #uuid "b8302ddf-29cf-570b-b7dd-dab545b3b824" :question/math-academy-id "q-162647" :question/problem "The domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡(t+\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,i+{e}^{t-1}\\,j+{t}^{2}\\,k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne .\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression? You may assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $\\operatorname{sec}⁡(t+\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ except for the values of $t$ for which\n\n$$\nt+\\frac{\\pi }{4}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi n\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\pi n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component ${e}^{t-1}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component ${t}^{2}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\pi n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-02673689-46fa-584e-88ff-1a1c967a1b0b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-02673689-46fa-584e-88ff-1a1c967a1b0b" :answer-field/id #uuid "02673689-46fa-584e-88ff-1a1c967a1b0b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-54811e57-5329-5901-9031-55945bdb3aaf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-976cc8f2-04f3-53c2-a86c-c645ed2fbec5" "answer-6d5d9399-1eaf-57c4-b24e-dd1b89bcd1e1" "answer-656b42d3-126c-5abb-9880-9e0fc6a9e621" "answer-da650f9b-762e-5944-b6e9-28cdf4865151" "answer-54811e57-5329-5901-9031-55945bdb3aaf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-976cc8f2-04f3-53c2-a86c-c645ed2fbec5" :answer/id #uuid "976cc8f2-04f3-53c2-a86c-c645ed2fbec5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi n}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6d5d9399-1eaf-57c4-b24e-dd1b89bcd1e1" :answer/id #uuid "6d5d9399-1eaf-57c4-b24e-dd1b89bcd1e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi n}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-656b42d3-126c-5abb-9880-9e0fc6a9e621" :answer/id #uuid "656b42d3-126c-5abb-9880-9e0fc6a9e621" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2\\pi n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-da650f9b-762e-5944-b6e9-28cdf4865151" :answer/id #uuid "da650f9b-762e-5944-b6e9-28cdf4865151" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi n}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-54811e57-5329-5901-9031-55945bdb3aaf" :answer/id #uuid "54811e57-5329-5901-9031-55945bdb3aaf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\pi n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7a104075-f533-58ab-b79b-2a5e66b667e2" :question/id #uuid "7a104075-f533-58ab-b79b-2a5e66b667e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-162660" :question/problem "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=⟨{e}^{-t},\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component ${e}^{-t}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\frac{1}{t}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,0)\\cup (0,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)$ is $t\\in (-1,\\infty ).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/a5/a55ef2c927b26c9beba9b44f669c817cf749b79de163b4bf0505d15c6ec31630.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is $t\\in (-1,0)\\cup (0,\\infty ).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-02381afc-745d-58f1-8f0d-9b55ea92ca31"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-02381afc-745d-58f1-8f0d-9b55ea92ca31" :answer-field/id #uuid "02381afc-745d-58f1-8f0d-9b55ea92ca31" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1000e325-da05-5f3a-9e1d-24312518777d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-94b764b3-edc6-585d-9049-19b093287871" "answer-1000e325-da05-5f3a-9e1d-24312518777d" "answer-691ebfd7-4000-5575-996f-d102ad66730b" "answer-2478ad2d-b6eb-59d1-b76b-abe7a69ec247" "answer-b312f764-3451-5f4e-9cfb-871263b18b8d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-94b764b3-edc6-585d-9049-19b093287871" :answer/id #uuid "94b764b3-edc6-585d-9049-19b093287871" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in (-1,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1000e325-da05-5f3a-9e1d-24312518777d" :answer/id #uuid "1000e325-da05-5f3a-9e1d-24312518777d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in (-1,0)\\cup (0,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-691ebfd7-4000-5575-996f-d102ad66730b" :answer/id #uuid "691ebfd7-4000-5575-996f-d102ad66730b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in (-1,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2478ad2d-b6eb-59d1-b76b-abe7a69ec247" :answer/id #uuid "2478ad2d-b6eb-59d1-b76b-abe7a69ec247" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in (-\\infty ,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b312f764-3451-5f4e-9cfb-871263b18b8d" :answer/id #uuid "b312f764-3451-5f4e-9cfb-871263b18b8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in (0,1)\\cup (1,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-d63840d2-3609-5c32-bdc9-4fe9ce0a42cd" :activity/id #uuid "d63840d2-3609-5c32-bdc9-4fe9ce0a42cd" :acti